    "created_at": "2017-08-30T14:33:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-08-30T14:33:00Z",
    "body": "Adding `noopener` to the `<form>` element seems like a relatively straightforward improvement, though it does open up the question of what other `rel` attributes should be exposed there.\r\n\r\nMy first concern about the `<base>` element would be that a page which had set `<base rel=\"noopener\">` would have no way to specify a link as one which is not `noopener`. I'm not sure if that's a use case which we want/need to support however.\r\n\r\nI'm also curious about `<base>`'s interaction with `window.open`, if you write `window.open(\"https://google.com\")` in a `<base rel=\"noopener\">` page, for example, one might expect the newly opener window to not have `window.opener` set, and for `window.open` to return `null`.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
